 "final_passage": "Marten-GNN achieved higher mean test accuracy than Pinecrest-Conv on Elmstead-Cite (84.7% vs 83.1%) and Harlow-Coauthor (92.6% vs 91.8%), but Pinecrest-Conv achieved higher mean accuracy on Brack-Social (70.4% vs 69.8%) and Tiller-Protein (76.2% vs 75.5%). Thus, the comparison is mixed across the four graphs, and the evidence does not support a claim that Marten-GNN generally outperforms Pinecrest-Conv on this benchmark. Marten-GNN did, however, exceed the feature-only MLP on all four graphs (84.7% vs 74.2%, 92.6% vs 88.9%, 69.8% vs 61.3%, and 75.5% vs 68.7%, respectively). No statistical tests were reported, so these differences are descriptive only.",
